digraph call_graph {
  // 453 of 1863 call records rendered, of which 0 are an identifier PASSED AS AN ARGUMENT and not a call at that site (dashed, and their tooltip says so); 453 are call sites. No render budget applies here, but only calls whose caller AND callee are both known source entities are kept (calls into libraries are dropped). The .mmd/.puml siblings are a different, budget-limited graph and they key their nodes by BARE NAME, so their node count is not this one.
  // 308 nodes: 306 resolved to ONE definition (file::qualified_name, the caller pinned by the span containing the call site) and 2 AMBIGUOUS -- a name several definitions carry, drawn dashed, its tooltip listing the sites and naming none. An edge touching an ambiguous node is attributed to the name, not to one definition.
  // 1 of the resolved nodes are not a callable -- a module or a class is the only entity carrying that name. They are drawn as a note and labelled, because a call graph node that is a file is not a thing the code calls.
  rankdir=LR;
  node [shape=box,style=filled,fillcolor="#1a3a5c",fontcolor=white,fontname="Helvetica",fontsize=9];
  edge [color="#666666"];
